1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,650
How do you pay for your coffee?
你怎样付款买咖啡呢？

2
00:00:02,650 --> 00:00:04,350
Is it with change?
是用零钱吗？

3
00:00:04,350 --> 00:00:07,580
I use my tap-and-go card.
我用我的感应式支付卡。

4
00:00:07,580 --> 00:00:13,680
I don't even need to enter my PIN number or a signature to authorise payment.
我甚至不需要输入个人密码或签名来授权付款。

5
00:00:13,680 --> 00:00:18,360
It's quicker and everybody in the queue is happy.
这样更快，而且排队的每个人都很高兴。

6
00:00:18,360 --> 00:00:22,310
Contactless payments are gaining popularity.
非接触式支付越来越受欢迎。

7
00:00:22,310 --> 00:00:33,470
Those concerned about security will be pleased to know that the amount of money you can spend in one go is limited - in the UK it's currently £30.
那些担心安全问题的人会很高兴知道，你一次可以消费的金额是有限制的——在英国，目前是30英镑。

8
00:00:33,470 --> 00:00:39,690
But if the card is used a few times in a row, a PIN number will be needed.
但如果这张卡连续使用几次，就需要输入个人密码了。

9
00:00:39,690 --> 00:00:47,150
If a thief gets hold of your card and goes on a spending spree, your bank covers you against fraud.
如果小偷拿到了你的卡并进行疯狂消费，你的银行会为你承担欺诈造成的损失。

10
00:00:47,150 --> 00:00:52,840
Whereas, if someone steals your banknotes, that's your bad luck!
然而，如果有人偷了你的纸币，那你就倒霉了！

11
00:00:52,840 --> 00:01:05,660
For those who are always forgetting where they put their cards, there's a new solution: wearable tech: clothing and accessories that have integrated electronic technology.
对于那些总是忘记把卡放在哪里的人来说，有一个新的解决方案：可穿戴技术，即集成了电子技术的服装和配饰。

12
00:01:05,660 --> 00:01:19,420
Kenneth Cukier, an economist and technology expert, says: "You can simply take any wireless card and the chip from it that your bank might issue you with, and you can put it in a coat.
经济学家兼技术专家肯尼斯·库基尔说：“你可以简单地取出银行发给你的任何一张无线卡及其芯片，然后把它放进一件外套里。

13
00:01:19,420 --> 00:01:27,575
When you want to make a payment just wave your arm in front of the terminal and leave the coffee shop with your latte.
当你想付款时，只需在终端机前面挥一挥手臂，然后就可以拿着你的拿铁离开咖啡店了。

14
00:01:27,575 --> 00:01:35,280
This is intended for people who don't want to take their card out of their wallet, use their phone or their watch."
这是为那些不想从钱包里拿出卡，也不想用手机或手表付款的人设计的。”

15
00:01:35,280 --> 00:01:37,530
Good, isn't it?
很棒，不是吗？

16
00:01:37,530 --> 00:01:41,140
And new ways of spending money are not stopping there.
而且新的支付方式还不止于此。

17
00:01:41,140 --> 00:01:44,670
The future is all about biometrics.
未来是生物识别技术的天下。

18
00:01:44,670 --> 00:02:02,390
Very convenient if you are at the beach or a festival - there's a new system in development which will make it possible to read the unique maps of veins under the surface of your finger, and use them to authenticate payments - or prove that it's you making the payments.
如果你在海滩或参加节日活动，这会非常方便——有一种正在开发的新系统，它将能够读取你手指表面下独特的静脉纹路图，并利用它们来验证付款，也就是证明是你在进行付款。

19
00:02:02,390 --> 00:02:07,110
You just need to remember which finger you registered with.
你只需要记住你是用哪根手指注册的就行了。

20
00:02:07,110 --> 00:02:10,840
So spending money is becoming easier all the time.
所以花钱总是变得越来越容易了。

21
00:02:10,840 --> 00:02:14,140
And the temptation to buy more stuff increases.
而且购买更多东西的诱惑也增加了。

22
00:02:14,140 --> 00:02:21,880
But it's worth bearing in mind that earning the money in the first place will still require the same effort.
但值得注意的是，首先要赚到钱，这仍然需要付出同样的努力。

23
00:02:21,880 --> 00:02:23,580
Back to work then!
那就回去工作吧！
